.br
.B tree -o file
.br
.B tree --charset set
.br
.B tree --timefmt fmt
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tree
tree lists a directory recursively with line drawing, like tree(1). Output matches tree v2.3.2 byte for byte for the options above; -H, -S, -A, --fromfile, --gitignore, --du, --inodes and --device are not implemented and are rejected with a message.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -a
list hidden files
.TP
.B -d
directories only
.TP
.B -l
follow symlinks
.TP
.B -f
print the full path of each file
.TP
.B -x
stay on this filesystem
.TP
.B -L level
descend only level directories deep
.TP
.B -P pattern
list only files matching pattern
.TP
.B -I pattern
leave out files matching pattern
.TP
.B --prune
drop empty directories
.TP
.B --matchdirs
apply -P to directories too
.TP
.B --ignore-case
case-insensitive patterns
.TP
.B --filelimit n
do not open directories with more than n entries
.TP
.B -p
show permissions
.TP
.B -u
show owner
.TP
.B -g
show group
.TP
.B -s
show size in bytes
.TP
.B -h
show size, human readable
.TP
.B --si
like -h with powers of 1000
.TP
.B -D
show modification date
.TP
.B -F
append / * @ = | to names
.TP
.B -i
no indentation lines
.TP
.B -q
print non-printable characters as ?
.TP
.B -N
print names raw
.TP
.B -Q
quote names
.TP
.B -C
colorize using LS_COLORS
.TP
.B -n
no color
.TP
.B -r
reverse the sort
.TP
.B -t
sort by modification time
.TP
.B -c
sort by status change time
.TP
.B -U
do not sort
.TP
.B -v
